/*!
\page build_and_run_example_12 Build and run Example 12

This page points to the standard Delft3D build instructions and the example run instructions for the
preC-SUMO / D-Flow FM coupling case in Example 12.

\section build_compile Build and compile Delft3D

The canonical build documentation lives in the project docs folder:
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/doc/compiling_Windows.md">Building Delft3D on Windows</a>
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/doc/compiling_Linux.md">Building Delft3D on Linux</a>

The repository-level build scripts are also the starting point for local builds:
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/run_conan.py">run_conan.py</a>
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/build.py">build.py</a>

In practice the usual workflow is:
1. configure the Conan environment,
2. run the repository build script,
3. build the required binaries and then use the generated executables from the install tree.

\section run_example_12 Run Example 12

The example case is located here:
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/readme.md">Example 12: D-Flow FM / preC-SUMO</a>

\dotfile preciceconfig_example12.dot "Example 12 preCICE Config"

That example contains the configuration and launch scripts for both coupled workflows:
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/dimr_config.xml">dimr_config.xml</a> for the DIMR-based run,
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/precice_config.xml">precice_config.xml</a> for the preCICE-based run,
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/run.bat">run.bat</a> / <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/run.sh">run.sh</a> for the preCICE workflow,
- <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/run_parallel.bat">run_parallel.bat</a> / <a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/run_parallel.sh">run_parallel.sh</a> for the parallel variant.

\section run_nf2ff_matrix_wrapper_windows Windows NF2FF matrix wrapper script

For Windows test-matrix runs, Example 12 also provides
<a href="https://github.com/Deltares/Delft3D/blob/main/examples/dflowfm/12_dflowfm_pre_C_SUMO/run_nf2ff_matrix_wrapper.bat">run_nf2ff_matrix_wrapper.bat</a>.
This wrapper repeatedly calls <code>run.bat</code> for selected NF2FF cases and run modes, depending on the case related NF2FF files being present.

Supported usage:
- <code>run_nf2ff_matrix_wrapper.bat [case_list] [mode]</code>
- <code>case_list</code>: one case or comma-separated cases (if omitted, all predefined cases are run)
- <code>mode</code>: <code>precice</code>, <code>dimr</code>, <code>both</code>, or <code>cleanupOnly</code>

What it does:
- validates requested case XML files exist under <code>cosumo/NF2FF</code>,
- performs cleanup (with confirmation, unless <code>AUTO_CONFIRM_DELETE=1</code>),
- runs each selected case in the selected mode(s),
- writes logs under <code>results/logs</code>,
- writes artifacts under <code>results/&lt;case&gt;/&lt;mode&gt;[ _timestamp ]</code>,
- creates summary files (<code>summary.csv</code> and <code>matrix.md</code>) for multi-case runs.

The example uses the same pattern as the project scripts:
- preCICE coupling starts preC-SUMO and D-Flow FM from the example directory,
- the DIMR option runs the DIMR configuration when the preCICE route is not selected.

\section results Compare results

Once the run completes, results can be compared in the user's preferred tooling:
- Delft3D Q-Plot,
- NetCDF comparison tools,
- or any other output diff / validation workflow the user chooses.

This page is intentionally kept brief; it points to the canonical build and example documentation rather than repeating the detailed comparison procedures.
*/
